---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const secretExample = "1011";
const guessExample = "1101";
---

<Layout title="How to Play">
	<div class="page-intro">
		<h1>How to Play</h1>
		<p>LogicDash and Overclocked are binary guessing games. Here's the whole rulebook.</p>
	</div>

	<div class="rules">
		<section class="rule">
			<h2>1. Making a guess</h2>
			<p>
				Tap the bit buttons to flip each one between <code>0</code> and <code>1</code>, building a
				binary string the same length as the secret — 5 bits in LogicDash, 6 bits in Overclocked.
				Press <strong>Guess</strong> to submit it.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rule">
			<h2>2. Reading the result</h2>
			<p>
				After each guess you get one number: how many bits <strong>differ</strong> from the secret.
				This is the <em>Hamming distance</em>. Lower is closer — <code>0</code> means an exact match.
			</p>
			<p>
				The game only ever tells you <strong>how many</strong> bits are wrong, never <strong>which
				ones</strong>. Narrowing that down guess by guess is the whole puzzle.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rule">
			<h2>3. Worked example</h2>
			<p>Say the hidden secret is <code>{secretExample}</code> and you guess <code>{guessExample}</code>:</p>
			<p class="example-note">
				(Shown side by side here for teaching — in an actual game you never see the secret until
				you match it or run out of attempts.)
			</p>
			<div class="example">
				<div class="example-row">
					<span class="example-label">Secret</span>
					<div class="example-tiles">
						{secretExample.split("").map((bit) => <span class="example-tile">{bit}</span>)}
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="example-row">
					<span class="example-label">Guess</span>
					<div class="example-tiles">
						{
							guessExample.split("").map((bit, i) => (
								<span class={`example-tile ${bit !== secretExample[i] ? "example-tile--diff" : ""}`}>
									{bit}
								</span>
							))
						}
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p>
				Positions 2 and 3 differ (<code>0↔1</code> and <code>1↔0</code>); the other two match. The
				game would report <strong>2 bits off</strong> — nothing more.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="rule">
			<h2>4. Attempts</h2>
			<p>
				You get 6 guesses per game, Wordle-style. Run out without matching and the secret is
				revealed — hit <strong>Play Again</strong> to get a fresh one instantly, no reload needed.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-intro {
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.page-intro h1 {
		margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2rem);
	}

	.page-intro p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.rules {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}

	.rule {
		background: var(--color-surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 16px;
		padding: 1.1rem 1.35rem;
	}

	.rule h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
	}

	.rule p {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}

	.rule p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.example-note {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.rule code {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		background: var(--color-surface-alt);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.rule strong {
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.example {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin: 0.75rem 0;
	}

	.example-row {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.example-label {
		width: 4rem;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.example-tiles {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.4rem;
	}

	.example-tile {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2.2rem;
		height: 2.2rem;
		border-radius: 8px;
		border: 1px solid #363c52;
		background: var(--color-surface-alt);
		color: #ced2e2;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
	}

	.example-tile--diff {
		border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-danger) 55%, transparent);
		color: var(--color-danger);
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-danger) 14%, var(--color-surface-alt));
	}
</style>
